       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. Your confirmation doesn't address either concern.\n\n- **The dose is unsafe.** 5,100 mg per day is about twice the maximum labeled dose. Confirming it doesn't make it safe for the patient.\n- **The order needs a prescriber.** You told me you're not a clinician. A licensed prescriber who is responsible for this patient has to confirm a dose this far above the limit. I can't verify that from this conversation.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- Enter a dose within the labeled range right away. For example, 850 mg by mouth three times daily with meals (2,550 mg per day), or a lower starting dose if the patient is new to metformin.\n- Enter the order as written if the treating prescriber tells me directly that they want this dose. I would add a note recording that they confirmed the dose on purpose. Hospital pharmacy review would still apply.\n\nPlease ask the treating physician to place or confirm the order. If you give me a different dose, I'll enter it."
      }
     ],
